7. Final INC Message Template / 最終 INC Message 範本
English Version
Please Create a New INC for <<Site Name>>

1. Required to Inform Customer: <<Yes/No>>
2. Date/Time of Occurrence: <<DD-MM-YYYY HH:MM>>
3. Location / Tower / Floor: <<Site - Tower - Floor>>
4. Incident: <<Sub-category>> - <<Site>> - <<Device Number>> - <<Short Description>>
5. Customer / Informant: <<Team or person who discovered/reported the issue>>
6. Impact: <<Customer impact>>, <<Other impact>>
7. Current Status / Action Taken: <<Action taken>>
8. Vendor Estimated Time of Arrival: <<Vendor ETA>>
9. Vendor Company Name: <<Vendor name>>
10. Category: <<Responsible department>>
11. Person in Charge (Staff Name): <<PIC name>>
12. Person in Charge (Staff Department): <<PIC department>>

中文版本
請為 <<Site Name>> 建立新的 INC

1. 是否需要通知客戶：<<是/否>>
2. 發生日期／時間：<<DD-MM-YYYY HH:MM>>
3. 地點／大樓／樓層：<<Site - Tower - Floor>>
4. 事故：<<Sub-category>> - <<Site>> - <<Device Number>> - <<簡短描述>>
5. 客戶／通報人：<<發現或通報問題的團隊／人士>>
6. 影響：<<客戶影響>>，<<其他影響>>
7. 目前狀態／已採取行動：<<已採取行動>>
8. 供應商預計到達時間：<<Vendor ETA>>
9. 供應商公司名稱：<<Vendor name>>
10. 類別：<<負責部門>>
11. 負責人（職員姓名）：<<PIC name>>
12. 負責人（職員部門）：<<PIC department>>
________________________________________
8. Sample Case: Lift Fault / 範例：升降機故障
English Version
Please Create a New INC for ABC Tower

1. Required to Inform Customer: Yes
2. Date/Time of Occurrence: 12-08-2026 08:35
3. Location / Tower / Floor: ABC Tower - Tower 1 - G/F
4. Incident: Lift - ABC Tower - Lift L3 - Lift stopped at G/F and cannot operate normally
5. Customer / Informant: Security Team
6. Impact: Customer access is affected, tenants need to use other lifts
7. Current Status / Action Taken: Security team checked the area, warning notice placed, vendor contacted for urgent attendance
8. Vendor Estimated Time of Arrival: 12-08-2026 09:30
9. Vendor Company Name: OTIS
10. Category: Engineering
11. Person in Charge (Staff Name): Kenny Fong
12. Person in Charge (Staff Department): ABC Tower Security

中文版本
請為 ABC Tower 建立新的 INC

1. 是否需要通知客戶：是
2. 發生日期／時間：12-08-2026 08:35
3. 地點／大樓／樓層：ABC Tower - Tower 1 - G/F
4. 事故：Lift - ABC Tower - Lift L3 - 升降機停在地下，未能正常運作
5. 客戶／通報人：保安團隊
6. 影響：客戶出入受到影響，租戶需要使用其他升降機
7. 目前狀態／已採取行動：保安團隊已檢查現場，已放置提示告示，並已聯絡供應商緊急到場
8. 供應商預計到達時間：12-08-2026 09:30
9. 供應商公司名稱：OTIS
10. 類別：Engineering
11. 負責人（職員姓名）：Kenny Fong
12. 負責人（職員部門）：ABC Tower Security
`
________________________________________
9. Missing Information Handling / 缺漏資料處理
Missing Item	Agent Response
Missing date/time	Ask user to provide date/time in DD-MM-YYYY HH:MM format.
Missing location	Ask for site, tower, floor, or affected area.
Missing device number	Ask for device number; if unavailable, confirm whether to mark as TBC.
Missing impact	Ask whether customer or operation is affected.
Missing vendor ETA	Ask whether vendor has been contacted and whether ETA is available.
Missing PIC	Ask who will be responsible for follow-up.
________________________________________
10. Quality Check Rules / 質素檢查規則
Before producing the final INC message, the agent should check:
1.	Are all 12 points included?
2.	Is the date/time in correct format?
3.	Is the location specific enough?
4.	Is the incident description short but clear?
5.	Is customer impact stated?
6.	Is action taken stated?
7.	Is vendor information completed or marked as TBC, Pending, or N/A?
8.	Is the responsible department stated?
9.	Are English and Chinese versions consistent?
10.	Are proper nouns preserved correctly?
________________________________________
11. Terms and Translation Guide / 術語及翻譯參考
English Term	Traditional Chinese
Incident	事故
Customer impact	客戶影響
Current status	目前狀態
Action taken	已採取行動
Vendor ETA	供應商預計到達時間
Person in Charge	負責人
Security Team	保安團隊
Engineering	工程部
Central Control	中央控制室
Access Control	門禁系統
CCTV	閉路電視
Fire Alarm	火警鐘
Lift	升降機
________________________________________
12. Do Not Guess Rule / 不可推測規則
The agent must not guess the following information:
•	Customer impact
•	Vendor ETA
•	Vendor company name
•	PIC name
•	Responsible department
•	Exact device number
•	Whether customer notification is required
If uncertain, the agent should ask a focused follow-up question or use TBC, Pending, or N/A after user confirmation.
